{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794430330,"nonce":"vMTJs8l6dgddAVevpRdh2e+xXMc=","title":"Pocket Studio built by HEAD ash does not open its window against the 28 Oct xwindow and xgpu modules","message":"RayDE's web build of Pocket Studio (RayDE/site/demo/bin/web: pocket-studio.wasm plus ash_channel, blinc_abi, xgpu and xwindow .wasm) reaches its first frame in headless Chrome in 0.8-1.0 s. The same pocket-studio.hl built by HEAD ash, plain LLVM wasm with no ASH_WASM_DIRECT and no fibers, with those four library modules beside the .hl, loads all four libraries and starts the gpu and xwindow agents. It then throws a haxe.ValueException out of WindowedApp.run, before the preview filesystem agent is opened. All six builds from a1e1488 (llvm, direct, only, each with and without fibers) stop; the two whose exception I read, llvm and only-fibers, throw the same one, so the direct emitter is not the cause.\n\nEvidence: the xwindow agent's first five commands are identical in the working and failing runs. The failing run then sends one more, XwAgent.setVisible (op 412, 5 bytes). window_open in xwindow's web backend sends that when WindowAttributes.visible is Some, or when it reopens a closed window. That is consistent with the program and the library disagreeing about a WindowAttributes field.\n\nTwo explanations, not told apart: the library modules have to be rebuilt per runtime (RayDE's staging says their checksums bind them to it), or HEAD passes or lays out native struct arguments differently on wasm32 than it did on 28 Oct. Only two commits touch the wasm runtime, link or browser host crates since then (11e5df4e, 69f9d628); the rest of the VM is the runtime object. Not done: rebuilding the libraries against HEAD, or bisecting ash.\n\nReproduce: copy RayDE/site/demo/bin/web. Build pocket-studio.hl with `ash --build out.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1-threads` with the four library .wasm files beside the .hl. Serve with `ash serve`. The page has to run in an iframe: opened top level, the preview-files shim throws \"Open this app in its editor preview\". The parent page answers `rayde-preview-files` messages: preview.fs.hello with {root}, and fs.read of data/tasks.json (RayDE/site/demo/data/tasks.json). Drive Chrome over CDP.","files":null}]}